        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string>Patch a Z SQL Method of the SQL catalog: src and/or arguments_src, applied\n
together through one manage_edit so the parsed _arg stays in sync (session\n
issue B9: editing only one of the two desynchronises it).\n
\n
Exact-match replacements (must match exactly once unless replace_all=true) are\n
supported for short single-line edits; multi-line changes are safer as a full\n
src rewrite (src / src_file) because pattern payloads get mangled by the JSON\n
transport. After any failed writing sequence, re-read the deployed source\n
(erp5_catalog_method_read) before retrying pattern edits.\n
\n
An accidental connection_id change is refused unless force_connection=true.\n
A failed manage_edit leaves the method untouched (no half-applied state).\n
The response echoes the post-write state (src_sha256 / arguments_sha256 let\n
you verify byte-exact deployment against local files), or status=\'noop\' when\n
the passed content already matches what is deployed.</string> </value>
